DusdPegCurveOracle::setRuntimeConfig(DusdPegCurveOracleRuntimeConfig)
├── given caller is not the current owner
│   ├── it should revert with OwnableUnauthorizedAccount(caller)
│   ├── it should leave both approved values unchanged
│   └── it should not emit SetRuntimeConfig
├── given caller is the pending owner but has not accepted ownership
│   ├── it should revert with OwnableUnauthorizedAccount(caller)
│   ├── it should leave both approved values unchanged
│   └── it should not emit SetRuntimeConfig
└── given caller is the current owner
    ├── when either proposed value is zero
    │   └── it should revert with DusdPegCurveOracleInvalidConfig
    ├── when ma_exp_time cannot be read
    │   └── it should bubble the pool revert
    ├── when ma_exp_time differs from newExpectedMaExpTime
    │   └── it should revert with DusdPegCurveOracleInvalidMaExpTime
    ├── when A_precise or future_A cannot be read
    │   └── it should bubble the pool revert
    ├── when A_precise or future_A differs from newExpectedAPrecise
    │   └── it should revert with DusdPegCurveOracleInvalidAmplification
    └── when both proposed values match the pool's current state
        ├── it should replace runtimeConfig atomically
        ├── it should allow subsequent matching pool observations
        ├── it should preserve ownership state
        └── it should emit SetRuntimeConfig(newRuntimeConfig)
